{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.FiniteTypeInvariant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.FiniteTypeInvariant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.WeightSystem","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finsupp.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.symbol_succ_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.symbol_succ_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L181-L185","doc":"One order below its order, a finite-type invariant's symbol vanishes:\nan order-`≤ m` invariant is annihilated on `(m+1)`-singular objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.symbol_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.symbol_add","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L176-L179","doc":"The symbol is additive in the invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.symbol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.symbol","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L172-L174","doc":"The degree-`m` symbol of an invariant: its extension restricted to\n`m`-singular objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.finiteTypeSubmodule_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.finiteTypeSubmodule_mono","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L157-L161","doc":"**The Vassiliev filtration.** The order-`≤ m` invariants are nested. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.mem_finiteTypeSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.mem_finiteTypeSubmodule","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L154-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.finiteTypeSubmodule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.finiteTypeSubmodule","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L147-L152","doc":"The submodule of order-`≤ m` finite-type invariants inside `K → R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType.smul","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L139-L144","doc":"Finite-type invariants of order `≤ m` are closed under scalar\nmultiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType.add","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L133-L137","doc":"Finite-type invariants of order `≤ m` are closed under addition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.isFiniteType_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.isFiniteType_zero","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L129-L131","doc":"The zero invariant has every finite order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType.mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType.mono","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L122-L127","doc":"Order is monotone: an order-`≤ m` invariant is also order-`≤ m'` for\n`m ≤ m'` (vanishing on `> m` double points implies vanishing on `> m'`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.IsFiniteType","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L115-L118","doc":"`v : K → R` is a **finite-type invariant of order ≤ m** when its extension\nvanishes on every singular object with more than `m` double points. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_desingularize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_desingularize","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L100-L111","doc":"The extension of a `(k+1)`-singular object is the difference of the\nextensions of its two `k`-singular smoothings — the first-difference\n(discrete-derivative) structure of the Vassiliev skein. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L95-L98","doc":"The zero invariant extends to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_smul","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L88-L93","doc":"`vExt` is homogeneous in the invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt_add","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L83-L86","doc":"`vExt` is additive in the invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.vExt","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L78-L81","doc":"The extension of an invariant `v : K → R` to a `k`-singular object: apply\n`v` `R`-linearly through the resolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.resolve_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.resolve_step","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The Vassiliev skein relation at the distinguished double point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.desingularize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.desingularize","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Resolve one distinguished double point into `(positive, negative)`\nsmoothings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.resolve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.resolve","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Full resolution into a signed formal sum of knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.Sing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.Sing","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L64-L64","doc":"`k`-fold singular objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Vassiliev.VassilievSetup","kind":"structure","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Vassiliev/FiniteTypeInvariant.lean#L50-L72","doc":"Data presenting the singular-knot resolution underlying finite-type theory\nfor a type `K` of knots.\n\n* `Sing k` — objects with exactly `k` transverse double points (`Sing 0 = K`\n  morally).\n* `resolve s` — the full resolution of every double point into a signed sum of\n  honest knots (the Vassiliev skein, applied at all `k` double points).\n* `desingularize s` — resolve *one* distinguished double point of a\n  `(k+1)`-singular object into its positive and negative smoothings, each a\n  `k`-singular object.\n* `resolve_step` — the skein relation at the distinguished double point:\n  `resolve s = resolve s₊ − resolve s₋`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}